## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, auditable CAPA design for IaC drift and nonconforming changes in a multi-tenant setup, plus concrete API, lifecycle, and metrics.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Evidence capture and auditability
- IaC drift detection and canary remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal API sketch for POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // store CAPA with req.body evidence
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'CAPA-123', ...req.body });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for audit logging and compliance needs?
- How would you prioritize CAPAs with conflicting remediation actions?

## Why This Is Asked

Covers a realistic data-leak risk from IAM misconfig in pipelines, focusing on formal CAPA processes at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- Evidence-driven REST APIs
- Metrics for containment and prevention
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Express route to POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const cap = { id: Date.now().toString(), ...req.body };
  caps.push(cap);
  res.status(201).json(cap);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you secure the CAPA API (authorization, audit logs, idempotency)?
- How would you integrate with existing incident response tools?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses capability to design scalable, tenant-aware CAPA for a shared data platform, balancing fairness and speed while ensuring traceability.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and backpressure control
- Evidence collection and artifact management
- Lifecycle state machine design
- REST API design for CAPA with logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics and RCA structuring
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

